{"tool_name":"kissplice","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"kissplice","identifiers":["doi:10.1093/nar/gkw655"],"license":"CeCILL","summary":"Detection of various kinds of polymorphisms in rna-seq data","home_url":"http://kissplice.prabi.fr/","keywords":["Amino Acid Sequence","Animals","Base Sequence","Computational Biology","Genetic Markers","Genome","Genomics","Genotype","Humans","Phenotype","Polymorphism, Single Nucleotide","Reproducibility of Results","Sequence Analysis, DNA","Sequence Analysis, RNA","Transcriptome","RNA-Seq"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":8564},"biotools":{"id":"KisSplice","home":"http://kissplice.prabi.fr","summary":"KisSplice is a software that enables to analyse RNA-seq data with or without a reference genome.","addition_date":"2019-11-06T11:29:56Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:18:29.063425Z","biotools_curie":"biotools:KisSplice","edit_permission":{"authors":["alexcorm"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Transcriptome assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3258"},{"term":"Variant calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3227"}]}],"name":"KisSplice","owner":"jison","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/1471-2105-13-s6-s5","metadata":{"abstract":"Background: In this paper, we address the problem of identifying and quantifying polymorphisms in RNA-seq data when no reference genome is available, without assembling the full transcripts. Based on the fundamental idea that each polymorphism corresponds to a recognisable pattern in a De Bruijn graph constructed from the RNA-seq reads, we propose a general model for all polymorphisms in such graphs. We then introduce an exact algorithm, called KISSPLICE, to extract alternative splicing events. Results: We show that KISSPLICE enables to identify more correct events than general purpose transcriptome assemblers. Additionally, on a 71 M reads dataset from human brain and liver tissues, KISSPLICE identified 3497 alternative splicing events, out of which 56% are not present in the annotations, which confirms recent estimates showing that the complexity of alternative splicing has been largely underestimated so far. Conclusions: We propose new models and algorithms for the detection of polymorphism in RNA-seq data. This opens the way to a new kind of studies on large HTS RNA-seq datasets, where the focus is not the global reconstruction of full-length transcripts, but local assembly of polymorphic regions. KISSPLICE is available for download at http://alcovna.genouest.org/kissplice/. \u00a9 2012 Sacomoto et al.","authors":[{"name":"Antoniou P."},{"name":"Chikhi R."},{"name":"Kielbassa J."},{"name":"Lacroix V."},{"name":"Peterlongo P."},{"name":"Sacomoto G.A.T."},{"name":"Sagot M.F."},{"name":"Uricaru R."}],"citationCount":82,"date":"2012-04-19T00:00:00Z","journal":"BMC Bioinformatics","title":"Kissplice: De-novo calling alternative splicing events from RNA-seq data"},"pmcid":"PMC3358658","pmid":"22537044"}],"topic":[{"term":"Genetic variation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0199"},{"term":"RNA-Seq","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3170"},{"term":"Transcriptomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3308"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"KisSplice","home":"https://bio.tools/KisSplice","summary":"KisSplice is a software that enables to analyse RNA-seq data with or without a reference genome.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:kissplice/undefined/kissplice.prabi.fr","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":56,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2024"},{"count":2,"year":"2022"},{"count":2,"year":"2023"},{"count":2,"year":"2026"},{"count":3,"year":"2013"},{"count":3,"year":"2025"},{"count":4,"year":"2015"},{"count":4,"year":"2016"},{"count":4,"year":"2017"},{"count":5,"year":"2018"},{"count":5,"year":"2021"},{"count":7,"year":"2014"},{"count":7,"year":"2019"},{"count":7,"year":"2020"}],"doi":"10.1186/1471-2105-13-S6-S5","pmcid":"PMC3358658","pmid":"22537044","ref_count":16,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"2002"},{"count":1,"year":"2004"},{"count":1,"year":"2010"},{"count":2,"year":"2001"},{"count":2,"year":"2009"},{"count":2,"year":"2011"},{"count":2,"year":"2012"},{"count":5,"year":"2008"}],"title":"KISSPLICE: de-novo calling alternative splicing events from RNA-seq data.","year":2012}]}],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":true,"license":false,"operational":200,"redirects":[{"status":301,"url":"https://kissplice.prabi.fr/"}],"ssl":true,"ssl_err":null}}},{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/bioconda:kissplice:2.4.0/cmd/kissplice.prabi.fr","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"bioconda","@type":"metrics","distribution":{"packages":true,"sourcecode":{}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":false,"osi":false},"publications":[],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":true,"license":false,"operational":200,"redirects":[{"status":301,"url":"https://kissplice.prabi.fr/"}],"ssl":true,"ssl_err":null}}},{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/bioconda:kissplice:2.4.0p1/cmd/kissplice.prabi.fr","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"bioconda","@type":"metrics","distribution":{"packages":true,"sourcecode":{}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":false,"osi":false},"publications":[],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":true,"license":false,"operational":200,"redirects":[{"status":301,"url":"https://kissplice.prabi.fr/"}],"ssl":true,"ssl_err":null}}},{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/bioconda:kissplice:2.5.5/cmd/